<title>USA: Cyclone Keli threatens shipping northeast of Fiji.</title>
<headline>Cyclone Keli threatens shipping northeast of Fiji.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Keli, with 120 mph winds, is well northeast of Fiji near 14s/175w and is a threat to shipping in the area, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Keli is moving southeast at 15 mph. It will accelerate and turn to the south, weakening during the next 36 hours.</p>
